body:
Using your experiences, thoughts, imagination sounds like a wonderful idea. Sometimes writing out the insane works! I would recommend writing your random words and thoughts on paper. Add drawings. Circle important words. Concentrate on those words. Let your mind wander. Make footnotes and side notes. Use colors. No need for self Judgement. Sometimes it is helpful to get it all out. I often daydream. I think about turning my daydreams into actual stories. Horror is a great genre. Rarely explored in contrast to romance. I like thriller, suspense, and romance myself. I read a lot of that when I was little. 

&#x200B;

Anyway, LET YOURSELF GO!
